dashboard-1  | 'server.enableCORS=false' tells Streamlit not to limit cross-origin access.
dashboard-1  | Streamlit sends the header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *', except on the file
dashboard-1  | upload routes, which stay pinned to the app address and still require a valid
dashboard-1  | XSRF token.
dashboard-1  | Streamlit also accepts a WebSocket connection from any origin.
dashboard-1  | Streamlit does not set 'server.enableCORS' to 'true' for you.
dashboard-1  | 'server.enableXsrfProtection=true' does not stop a cross-origin WebSocket
dashboard-1  | connection, because Streamlit does not need a valid XSRF token to open one.
dashboard-1  | 
dashboard-1  | To limit cross-origin access, do these steps:
dashboard-1  |   1. Set 'server.enableCORS=true'.
dashboard-1  |   2. Put the origins that you trust in 'server.corsAllowedOrigins'.
dashboard-1  | 
dashboard-1  | 'server.allowedHosts' can also limit the hostnames that Streamlit accepts on a
dashboard-1  | WebSocket connection.
